<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maria Komnene, Queen of Jerusalem</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1154–c. 1217</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Maria Comnena</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maria Komnene was a Byzantine princess, great-niece of Emperor Manuel I, who married King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amalric-i-of-jerusalem">Amalric I of Jerusalem</a> in 1167. She was the mother of Queen Isabella I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>. After Amalric's death in 1174 she married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balian-of-ibelin">Balian of Ibelin</a> and remained an influential figure in the politics of the crusader kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maria-komnene-queen-of-jerusalem.jpg" alt="Maria Komnene, Queen of Jerusalem" width="152" height="189" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MarieKomnene.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
